---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Cookies" description="Dustbound cookie policy — no first-party cookies or analytics.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6" data-testid="cookies-page">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-black text-ink">Cookie policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 10 August 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-muted" data-testid="cookies-body">
      <p data-testid="no-first-party-cookies">
        The Dustbound website at <a href="https://dustbound.app/">dustbound.app</a>
        <strong class="text-ink">does not set first-party cookies</strong> and
        <strong class="text-ink">does not use analytics</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because we do not use non-essential cookies or tracking scripts, we do not show a cookie consent banner.
      </p>
      <p>
        The interest signup form posts your email to Formspree so we can notify you about early release.
        That request is a cross-origin form submission; we do not load Formspree’s thank-you page when JavaScript is available.
        See the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> (Website section) and
        <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree’s Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        GitHub Pages (and any CDN such as Cloudflare in front of the site) may process standard technical connection data
        (for example IP address and User-Agent) when serving pages. That is hosting infrastructure, not Dustbound first-party cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we later add analytics or third-party challenge scripts, we will update this policy and add consent where required.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
